# Codex Governance

This project uses the Codex governance kit.

## Startup Order

1. Read `AGENTS.md` if it exists in the repository root.
2. Read `PROJECT.md`.
3. Read `rules/common/development-workflow.md` and `rules/common/git-workflow.md` when they exist.
4. Load task-specific references from `skills/` only when the request clearly matches.

## Execution Rules

- Run the repository health check before substantial work.
- Do not claim git state from memory.
- Treat `AGENTS.md`, `rules/*`, and `skills/*` as behavior assets.
- For semantic edits to behavior assets, keep verification evidence traceable in repository files.
- Preserve unrelated local changes.

## Platform Note

- This Cursor rule is the project-side entrypoint.
- If the project also installs the Codex global baseline, keep `~/.codex/AGENTS.md` and repository `AGENTS.md` aligned.
